      "Explanation": "諸佛出身處 is “the place from which the buddhas emerge,” a stock question in recorded encounters. The question is normally spoken by an unnamed monk, while different masters answer locally: “East Mountain walks on the water,” “a donkey womb and horse belly,” “you asked very fittingly,” and other incompatible replies. The corpus therefore fixes the interrogative formula but supplies no single shared place-name as its answer. Later raisers explicitly quote Yunmen’s question-and-answer as an inherited case."
